(6525537, 968917, 30982, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by h2:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Melethia:</b></div><hr/><i> I just so want to move that bottom right flower down and over just a wee bit....<br/> <br/>Good on you for keeping Timfy on his toes!!  But I gotta say that Christiane''s been doing better work than you the past few challenges.  :-) </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>No, it''s the bottom left that has to move up and right. Seriously, a little imperfection sometimes makes an image better... </i></td></tr></table> <br/>I don''t disagree.  In quilting (which I used to do), one always made a "mistake" somewhere because only God was capable of perfection, or so the story goes.  When I quilted, I made LOTS of mistakes, just to be sure...  <br/> <br/>In this case, maybe have one flower half out of the frame?  But then it wouldn''t be as Sherpet''ish that way.  Still, might make for an interesting photograph.</td>', 'Originally posted by h2: Originally posted by Melethia: I just so want to move that bottom right flower down and over just a wee bit.... Good on you for keeping Timfy on his toes!!  But I gotta say that Christiane''s been doing better work than you the past few challenges.  :-)   No, it''s the bottom left that has to move up and right. Seriously, a little imperfection sometimes makes an image better...  I don''t disagree.  In quilting (which I used to do), one always made a "mistake" somewhere because only God was capable of perfection, or so the story goes.  When I quilted, I made LOTS of mistakes, just to be sure...   In this case, maybe have one flower half out of the frame?  But then it wouldn''t be as Sherpet''ish that way.  Still, might make for an interesting photograph.', '2011-09-02 20:19:37.000000', NULL, 0),
